EmailValidator
==============

Validates that an attribute is an email address.

Installation
============

Add the gem to your Gemfile:

  gem "validation_kit"

Example
=======

class Person < ActiveRecord::Base
  validates :email, email: true
end

Person.new(email: "Bob").valid?             # false
Person.new(email: "joe@foobar.com").valid?  # true

Error Messages
==============

Invalid addresses get the standard :invalid error ("is invalid"). Pass a
:message option for a custom message:

  validates :email, email: { message: "doesn't look like an email address" }

or translate it with Rails' I18n system:

en:
  activerecord:
    errors:
      models:
        person:
          attributes:
            email:
              invalid: "Enter your email address"

(Use activemodel instead of activerecord for ActiveModel classes that aren't
ActiveRecord models.)


